1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:01,555
<i>Well, well.</i>

2
00:00:01,675 --> 00:00:03,796
Hunter.

3
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:08,521
Grant. Hey. Hunter, from Ops. We met
at… onboarding.

4
00:00:09,150 --> 00:00:11,874
Culture audit. Board's idea. Keep it
quiet.

5
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:13,556
Right. Ops.

6
00:00:13,676 --> 00:00:16,946
<i>Liar. The board doesn't have ideas. I
do.</i>

7
00:00:17,650 --> 00:00:21,176
Swing by twenty-two later. Let's talk
about your… department.

8
00:00:21,650 --> 00:00:23,930
Twenty-two?! What did you do?

9
00:00:24,650 --> 00:00:25,556
Spreadsheet thing.

10
00:00:28,650 --> 00:00:29,935
<i>Who calls on a Saturday?</i>

11
00:00:31,650 --> 00:00:35,416
Phone. In. Everything'll still be on
fire in an hour.

12
00:00:35,900 --> 00:00:37,826
<i>You have no idea what's on fire.</i>

13
00:00:40,900 --> 00:00:46,178
<i>Nothing to twist. Huh. When'd I last
hear myself breathe?</i>

14
00:00:46,650 --> 00:00:48,106
See? You didn't die.

15
00:00:48,650 --> 00:00:51,856
Okay, Ops. Happiest you've been all
year. Go.

16
00:00:52,650 --> 00:00:53,657
…This is pretty close.

17
00:00:55,650 --> 00:00:58,010
<i>Don't blush. It's a sauna. It's
allowed.</i>

18
00:00:58,650 --> 00:01:01,355
This was eighty-nine bucks. For two.

19
00:01:01,900 --> 00:01:02,873
Then I'm a cheap date.

20
00:01:02,993 --> 00:01:04,615
You eat chalk. I know.

21
00:01:05,900 --> 00:01:07,665
<i>Why am I telling him this?</i>

22
00:01:07,785 --> 00:01:12,170
Can I tell you something? Not weird.
Just… real.

23
00:01:12,650 --> 00:01:16,990
When I was twelve, my dad got laid
off. Twenty-two years.

24
00:01:17,650 --> 00:01:21,056
Fifteen-minute meeting. They gave him
a box and a parking validation.

25
00:01:22,650 --> 00:01:24,879
<i>Fifteen minutes. I've run those
meetings.</i>

26
00:01:26,650 --> 00:01:31,702
For a month he still put his boots on.
Every morning. Sat in the truck.

27
00:01:32,650 --> 00:01:37,502
He had a Lisbon jar. For my abuela. It
paid the light bill.

28
00:01:38,150 --> 00:01:41,000
The guy who signed it probably never
even knew his name.

29
00:01:43,150 --> 00:01:44,230
Abby. I—

30
00:01:46,150 --> 00:01:51,384
Anyway. That's why I send money home.
You'd never do that. To people.

31
00:01:51,900 --> 00:01:52,556
…No.

32
00:01:52,676 --> 00:01:54,234
<i>Liar.</i>

33
00:01:59,900 --> 00:02:02,910
<i>Two weeks, I said. He gave me one
night.</i>

34
00:02:03,900 --> 00:02:04,913
…Board vote?
